WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:04.663
If you are building your firm's next partners,
here is how to review them on evidence.

00:00:04.903 --> 00:00:13.265
One private equity firm spent 60 to 100 hours of senior time
trying to make a general AI assistant run its reviews.

00:00:13.505 --> 00:00:15.844
Then it gave up. Here is what it did instead.

00:00:16.444 --> 00:00:18.086
The firm had done the hard part.

00:00:18.326 --> 00:00:23.740
Its COO had written down, on one page, what
a great senior deal professional does.

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:28.969
But a framework on paper cannot interview anyone,
gather evidence or write a review.

00:00:29.569 --> 00:00:34.003
Ask yourself. Do your principals know where
they stand on each competency today?

00:00:34.243 --> 00:00:37.548
And could you show the evidence behind
your next partner-readiness call?

00:00:38.148 --> 00:00:40.161
We believe your framework is the asset.

00:00:40.401 --> 00:00:45.470
It needs a system that interviews your people,
gathers the evidence and drafts the write-up.

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:47.383
That is why we built CraftArc.

00:00:47.623 --> 00:00:52.908
CraftArc runs your review cycle on your own competency
framework, written in plain English.

00:00:53.508 --> 00:00:58.338
In the self-review, an AI coach interviews
each person against your competencies.

00:00:58.578 --> 00:01:04.644
People can talk to the agent by voice or text, and in the
self-review the coach asks for whatever is missing.

00:01:05.244 --> 00:01:10.872
Colleagues who worked with each person then give AI-led
interviews about what they saw first-hand.

00:01:11.112 --> 00:01:15.705
The agent grades every fact as directly
observed, hearsay or third party.

00:01:16.305 --> 00:01:21.785
The agent checks coverage for every competency and
flags the gaps before you complete the survey.

00:01:22.025 --> 00:01:26.613
Here, it warns that nobody who saw the banker
meetings has been heard on sourcing.

00:01:27.213 --> 00:01:32.069
Then it drafts the Executive Committee writeup,
the note to the person and the scorecard.

00:01:32.309 --> 00:01:36.842
Here, the writeup opens by naming the question
the evidence could not answer.

00:01:37.082 --> 00:01:41.574
The evaluation coordinator runs each
review and owns the final wording.

00:01:42.174 --> 00:01:46.819
The AI does not decide where someone
stands. Your evaluation coordinator

00:01:46.819 --> 00:01:49.980
forms the view with the agent, from graded facts.

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:56.122
The coach never nags. If someone does not want to answer,
it asks once or twice and then lets them go.

00:01:56.722 --> 00:02:04.702
The firm that gave up on its AI assistant then signed a 24-month
licence, and now runs its senior deal team on CraftArc.

00:02:04.942 --> 00:02:08.693
We built it with that firm's COO, who designed the framework.

00:02:08.933 --> 00:02:16.318
Our founder, Dash, worked at McKinsey, Microsoft and Siemens,
and builds AI agents for private equity deal teams.

00:02:16.918 --> 00:02:20.865
You start with your senior deal team only,
which keeps the disruption low.

00:02:21.105 --> 00:02:25.690
Participants and evaluators are unlimited,
and contributors are never charged.

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:32.924
If we miss a stage we agreed to deliver and do not fix it,
you can leave, and we refund your prepaid fees pro rata.

00:02:33.164 --> 00:02:39.507
It works best when leadership commits to running the cycle.
If that commitment is not there yet, we will say so.

00:02:40.107 --> 00:02:43.379
If your next review cycle starts in the new year, plan it now.

00:02:43.619 --> 00:02:49.052
Book a demo, bring your competency framework, and we
will talk through how it would run on CraftArc.

00:02:49.292 --> 00:02:51.153
This voice is AI generated.
